  "title": "National Party election victory of 1948 and the first apartheid laws",
  "summary": "In May 1948 the National Party, led by Daniel Malan and campaigning on apartheid, won South Africa's general election, taking 79 seats to the United Party's 71 although the United Party and its allies held more of the popular vote. Its government then passed laws enforcing racial separation, including the 1949 mixed-marriages ban and the 1950 Population Registration and Group Areas Acts.",
